{
  "spec": "REACTIONS-DESIGN.md revision 2: §1 FIELD_REACTION (0x40), §4 GROUP_POST_ID (0xD1 key 11), §5.2 SENT_HASH (0xD1 key 12), §5.3 post_id after left and the react op; RFed SPEC §17.14",
  "notes": [
    "Generated for Retichat-js (reactions.test.mjs checks it); the bytes are written as Python's umsgpack writes them (each int in its smallest form, fixstr/str 8, bin 8), by an encoder independent of msgpackr.",
    "group_sync: fields_hex is a G's fields map (0x0C, 0xFB, 0xFC, 0xFD); expected is the §7 group_sync reading with `content` and `post_id` added (null where an op has none; `problem` set and the rest null when refused: its text is the web's wording, and only whether it is null counts across readers). Entries with writer true are what a writer makes from `sync`; the web writes at_ms as an int 64 (0xd3), its one difference.",
    "reaction: payload_hex is an LXMF payload [timestamp, title, content, fields] whose fields are fields_hex; expected is the reading of 0x40: {reaction: null} when absent, {refused: true, not_a_map} when refused, else REACTION_TO's bytes as to_hex and REACTION_CONTENT as UTF-8.",
    "retichat_field: fields_hex is a fields map; expected is key 11 (a str of 32 hex, read lowercased) and key 12 (a str of 64 hex, read lowercased) of its 0xD1, null when absent or malformed."
  ],
